Subject: [PATCH 188/256] perf(timing): C6 W8A8 cuEvent evidence harness +
 vendor two-pass shim

Measurement-only tooling for the C6 CUDA W8A8 timing evidence task:

- scripts/perf/c6_timing_harness.py: cuEvent timing of the four frozen
  W8A8 opcodes on the 12 W8J GEMM shapes (48 cases), in-window cuEvent
  rate calibration (raw + corrected), warmup + R=21 rounds, ERR-0004
  outlier marking, dedicated wall-agreement batch, representative
  public-entry dispatch overhead, GPU window contamination sampling,
  and the two-pass comparison (cublasGemmEx int8->s32 + our C6
  epilogue) and bf16 platform baseline, including interleaved paired
  ratios.
- scripts/perf/c6_vendor_shim.c: header-checked C shim for classic
  cublasGemmEx; a direct ctypes call with the documented 19-argument
  signature was rejected on the GamePC CUDA 13.3 stack while the
  identical C call returns status 0.
- scripts/perf/c6_timing_analyze.py: ERR-0004 / variance / rate-gate
  analysis + markdown tables, all UNGATED.
- scripts/perf/c6_timing_selftest.py: local mock self-test of the
  launch mapping, buffer sizes, correctness checks and verdicts.
- scripts/perf/c6_timing_gamepc.sh: sync/run/fetch/clean runner for the
  shared GamePC (GPU-only, no gamepc lock, no residue).

No runtime/compiler/contract source is modified.
